\section{Detail levels (\code{recipient_type_detail})}{

A finer split carried alongside the standard, because \code{other_unknown} mixes
cases that behave very differently: \code{government} and \code{foreign} can never be in
the BMF, while \code{blank} and \code{unrecognized} are usually organizations the filer
simply did not code. Only the detail level is precise enough to drive the
out-of-sample decision — see \code{\link[=pf_oos_details]{pf_oos_details()}}.
